<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">conditions</ansi>

The <ansi fg="command">conditions</ansi> command lists everything currently affecting you,
grouped so you can see what matters at a glance:

  <ansi fg="yellow">Rest</ansi>          <ansi fg="command">Rested</ansi> or <ansi fg="command">Well Rested</ansi>, and the real time left on it.
  <ansi fg="yellow">Weapon edges</ansi>  A sharpened blade, and how many strikes its edge
                has left (<ansi fg="command">help sharpen</ansi>).
  <ansi fg="yellow">Survival</ansi>      Any need — hunger, thirst, fatigue — worth a
                warning, and your warmth if it's uncomfortable. An
                "In battle" row says what your needs and a meal buff
                do in the next fight (<ansi fg="command">help survival</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help cooking</ansi>).
  <ansi fg="yellow">Company</ansi>       Your company's chemistry tier, if you've served
                together long enough for one (<ansi fg="command">help chemistry</ansi>).
  <ansi fg="yellow">Other effects</ansi> Everything else affecting you, with time left
                where it has any.

A group with nothing in it is left out. If you have none of the above,
<ansi fg="command">conditions</ansi> simply says so.

See also: <ansi fg="command">help status</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help survival</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help sharpen</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help camp</ansi>,
<ansi fg="command">help inn</ansi>.


In the web client, Company > Status shows each owned member's active
effects and wounds separately from persistent bonuses. Character >
Effects shows the same details for you. An effect known to hurt you
(a weakening modifier, bleeding, poison, lost actions and the like) is
labelled Harmful; one known to help is labelled Helpful. Timed effects count
down in the panel with a bar showing the time left; combat-round effects
count combat rounds. Light wounds last until fight end; lasting
wounds remain until treatment or rest, rather than having a countdown.
Wounds hold back health and lower the healing limit (help wounds).
Away members with live state are marked away; otherwise effects are
unknown and wounds are only last recorded. Fallen members have no active
member effects. Another company's private conditions are never shown.
